# One C function, two modules, two contracts: this one says `keep` reads the
# bytes for the call and no longer, `alt.hero` says it keeps them. Each module
# is right against C alone and the two cannot both be right, which is what
# `contract_differs` says (M-agreed-retention's second item).
use alt

extern "keep.h"
    function keep(s: cstr lent)

function main()
    keep(s: "main".cstr())
    alt.keeping()
